cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these fixtures, cite LBFGSpp and Eigen, which produce them.
title: L-BFGS-B oracle generator (host-native test, not vendored)
abstract: >-
  gen.cpp is written here; nothing is vendored. build.sh clones
  V-Sekai-fire/interactor-aria-lbfgspp at the pinned commit into .deps/
  (gitignored) and compiles gen.cpp against its thirdparty/LBFGSpp/include
  (LBFGSpp 0.3.0, MIT; include/ byte-identical to the copy in
  cloth-dynamics external/LBFGSpp) and its thirdparty/eigen (Eigen 3.4.90,
  MPL-2.0). Both are used unmodified and only by this host-native tool, whose
  outputs are the text fixtures in gates/5-drape/oracle/; neither library is
  linked into any guest ELF. Local adaptation: gen.cpp wraps the LBFGSB.h
  include in `#define private public` to read LBFGSBSolver::max_step_size,
  proj_grad_norm and BFGSMat::m_ptr without copying or editing the headers.
type: software
authors:
  - name: V-Sekai-fire
  - name: chibifire
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-aria-lbfgspp
